    "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/",
    "note": "Kenney building-skyscraper-d, picked from the kit's five skyscrapers: the slimmest and tallest, a continuous glass curtain wall on all four sides with a sun-shade louvre at every floor, a glazed street lobby and a rooftop vent, which reads as a narrow Tokyo office tower (a and e are squat or blank-sided, b has no roof detail, c is only 7 office floors). FBX member plus its colormap texture, flattened to 20 colours, same recipe and indigo mapping as building-apartment so they read as one city. Height: a double-height lobby (about 8.5 m with its transfer band) and 11 office floors at ~3.7 m (measured from the louvre spacing), plus parapet and roof vent = 56 m; it is then 13.1 m wide and 14.2 m deep. Turned 180 degrees so the glazed entrance faces +Z (the kit has a service door there). Static, no clips. Indigo script: lit office glass (practical/iris), navy curtain-wall frames and cornices, pale spandrels and lobby band, near-black stone base and roof deck."
  },
